							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=813.msg11890#msg11890">Quote from: Gabus on October 20, 2004, 10:09:03 am</a></div><div class="quote">Sorry if this pisses on your self-importance, but honestly is it REALLY that important to remember who got the second, third, or beyond, epics? (assuming of course that it is important to know who got the first one.)<br /><br />As the great poet Nelly put it. (yes I am being sarcastic here)<br /><br />2 is not a winner...<br />3 no one remembers...<br /><br /></div><br />You sir, just became my new personal hero.<br /><br />Of course, some would argue that who got the first epic 2.0 is no where near as meaningful as the early accomplishments in EQ, seeing that 5-year old EQ is very &quot;old hat&quot; at this point.&nbsp; I know I kind of share that feeling.&nbsp; <br /><br />Does anyone else feel a lack of luster or even care about who finishes Tacvi first or who is the first to enter or clear Citadel of Anguish?&nbsp; &quot;Firsts&quot; just don&#039;t seem to pack the same punch as they did before the game became stale and we had already had probably 50 prior &quot;firsts&quot; of various accomplishments in EQ.&nbsp; After the 50th &quot;first&quot;, they just don&#039;t seem to mean as much.<br /><br />/shrug<br />&nbsp;
